When a style change asks for another kind of box, Ladybird keeps the
old style on the old box until the layout tree update replaces the box,
so no layout sees a box of one kind with the style of another. Blink
does the same: Element::RecalcOwnStyle() returns before it updates an
existing LayoutObject when the layout tree needs reattaching. Gecko’s
RestyleManager::ProcessPostTraversal() leaves a frame that needs
reconstructing with its old style, for the frame constructor to replace.
And WebKit’s RenderTreeUpdater::updateElementRenderer() tears the
renderers down before the new style reaches any renderer.
